Around **150,000 phones are blocked as lost or stolen in Australia every year**, and only about one in three is later unblocked because it made its way back to its owner. Many are snatched in busy places, often by thieves on e-bikes or e-scooters targeting people checking a map or taking a photo.

This guide is for Android phones. The first few minutes matter most: thieves often go straight for your bank accounts and payment apps, not just the phone. Here's what to do, in the right order.

<figure class="blog-figure" style="max-width: 540px;">
