## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Should I call 000 or 131 444 if my phone is stolen?
A: Call 000 if you've been hurt, feel unsafe or the theft is happening right now. Otherwise, call the Police Assistance Line on 131 444 or report it online through your state or territory police.

### Q: Does blocking my phone's IMEI cost anything?
A: No. Blocking a lost or stolen phone is free, and your provider shares the block with all Australian mobile networks.

### Q: Will a blocked phone still work overseas?
A: Possibly. The IMEI block only applies to Australian networks, and stolen phones are sometimes sent overseas. That's why it's also important to lock the phone remotely and change your passwords.

### Q: Can my provider track my stolen phone?
A: No. Mobile providers don't track or locate lost and stolen phones. Use Find Hub to see its location, and give that information to the police rather than going there yourself.

### Q: How can I check if a second-hand phone is stolen?
A: Enter its IMEI in AMTA's free IMEI checker before you buy it. A phone that has been reported lost or stolen won't work on Australian networks, and your provider can't unblock it for you.

### Q: Can CrookCatcher help me get my phone back?
A: CrookCatcher gives you evidence: a photo of the person who tried to unlock your phone, the time and the location, sent straight to your email. You can share this with the police to help identify the thief. It doesn't guarantee your phone will be recovered, but it gives you and the police much more to go on.

